{"type":"message","id":"5cc55ae5","parentId":"ce6f6aeb","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:57:38.152Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need to run the crypto news pipeline per SOUL.md. Steps: research, write, generate image, publish, final report. Must use <thinking> blocks before each exec to confirm command and ensure previous step succeeded.\n\nWe need to clear researcher session file, run openclaw agent command with deliver, capture JSON output to RESEARCH_JSON variable. Then inform user after each step.\n\nWe need to actually execute shell commands via exec tool. Use exec with command string. The commands involve file paths like ~/.openclaw/agents/researcher/sessions/sessions.json etc. Should be okay.\n\nWe need to capture output. exec returns output in tool response. We'll need to store it. We can't have variables across messages, but we can include in subsequent commands using shell variable? Better to capture to a file then read.\n\nFor research: we can run command that writes to a file, e.g., openclaw agent ... --deliver > /tmp/research.json. Then read that file.\n\nSOUL says: Save JSON output as RESEARCH_JSON. I think they expect variable; we can just store file.\n\nAlso need to remove sessions.json before each.\n\nAfter research, we need to tell user: \"✅ Research done, starting article...\"\n\nThen step 2: write. It runs writer command and writes to /tmp/crypto-article.md, then sanitizes thinking blocks, checks Word Count existence, possibly retry. Many commands chained; we can execute as a script via bash -c.\n\nBetter to execute a single bash script with multiple lines separated by && or newline.\n\nWe need to ensure we wait for each command's success.\n\nWe'll do exec with command that does everything, then read the article file.\n\nAfter writing, inform user: \"✅ Article written, generating image...\"\n\nStep 3: generate image. Need to extract fields from RESEARCH_JSON: topic_theme, combined_key_facts first 2 items, primary crypto asset. We need to parse JSON. Use jq maybe. Is jq installed? Might be. Could use python -c.\n\nSimplify: Use jq to extract. We'll create variables IMAGE_TOPIC, IMAGE_FACTS, IMAGE_ASSET. Then run creator agent command.\n\nThe creator command writes to some path? It likely returns output but not file. According to SOUL, creator returns a file path for image maybe saved as /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg. We need to capture that. Probably the creator agent will output something like a path or \"IMAGE_FAILED\". We'll capture output to variable.\n\nWe'll execute command and capture output to a file, e.g., /tmp/creator-output.txt. Then read it.\n\nAfter image generation, tell user \"✅ Image generated, publishing to Google Drive...\"\n\nStep 4: Publish. Need to embed image if path not IMAGE_FAILED, convert to docx, then run publisher agent command (gog drive upload) and capture JSON, extract webViewLink.\n\nWe'll need to parse JSON to get link, maybe using jq.\n\nFinally, final report.\n\nWe must use <thinking> blocks before each exec.\n\nImplement stepwise.\n\nLet's start with step 1.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_rJ49cDCVJ6GyLhYvYTJrZo","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/researcher/sessions/sessions.json && openclaw agent --agent researcher --message \"Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Return the aggregated Single-Topic JSON.\" --deliver > /tmp/research.json && cat /tmp/research.json","timeout":120}}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0","usage":{"input":10516,"output":736,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11252,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777874248365}}
