{"type":"message","id":"64a02c39","parentId":"f59e93fe","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:58:54.420Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It appears the file might be empty or not generated. Maybe the researcher agent failed. Let's check exit status? The exec didn't show errors. Maybe the agent wrote to stdout, but our redirect > /tmp/research.json captured output. Could be blank due to error. We need to see if researcher session logs. Use process logs? The exec was run in background; we can check its logs? The exec tool may store output already displayed. The completed response didn't show output. Maybe need to capture stdout via exec without redirection and read from exec result. Let's rerun but capture output to variable via exec returning stdout. Instead of redirect, we can just let exec output to console and capture using tool output. We can run again and capture.\n\nFirst, clear sessions again.<thinking>We will run researcher command again, without redirection, and capture output directly.</thinking>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_dQuYWtx3X2NzANgiucMXaZ","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/researcher/sessions/sessions.json && openclaw agent --agent researcher --message \"Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Return the aggregated Single-Topic JSON.\" --deliver","timeout":120}}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0","usage":{"input":11554,"output":272,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11826,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777874328741}}
