{"type":"message","id":"fe7b3adf","parentId":"6afb1d05","timestamp":"2026-05-04T06:01:05.810Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The researcher command got killed? Something may be hanging. Possibly the openclaw agent command requires interactive terminal? Might need to run with --deliver which returns output, but maybe it waits for user approval? Could be requiring approval to run external network fetch. The system may need approval for network calls. The openclaw agent may try to fetch RSS feeds and require network access, which may need approval. According to policy, exec may require approval. The tool may have returned an \"approval pending\" note. We didn't see that. The exec may have been killed due to policy.\n\nWe need to request user approval? The tool response didn't show command. The exec tool may respond with a message containing /approve command. We haven't seen it. Might need to look at exec output more. Let's run exec with a simpler command to see behavior. But time.\n\nMaybe better to use the curl fallback approach mentioned: If researcher fails, try curl -s 'https://decrypt.co/feed' etc. Could use curl to fetch RSS and then parse? That's complex.\n\nSimplify: We can inform user that researcher step failed due to needing approval, and ask to approve network access. Use the exec output to see needed approval command. Since we didn't see, maybe need to read process logs. Use process logs for session quick-dune.<reasoning>Get logs of the exec session to see any approval request.</reasoning>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_5x2m39pwMDHzi7xTHtIsLV","name":"process","arguments":{"action":"log","sessionId":"quick-dune","limit":2000}}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0","usage":{"input":11933,"output":328,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12261,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":177787445472