{"type":"message","id":"73774705","parentId":"93d2adb5","timestamp":"2026-05-04T06:01:13.423Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It seems the process didn't produce output before being killed.\n\nMaybe openclaw agent requires interactive input for network authentication. Could be need to set environment variable GOG_KEYRING_PASSWORD later for publisher step, but that's later.\n\nPossibly the researcher agent tries to fetch RSS which is external network; the sandbox may block network by default; need approval.\n\nWe should request user to approve a network request. The exec tool would have returned a command like \"/approve openclaw agent ...\". Since we didn't capture, we may need to re-run with a flag to request approval. However, the exec tool might automatically output approval request for each external command.\n\nLet's try running researcher command again with a simpler fetch: maybe using curl directly to get JSON? But we need aggregated JSON from researcher. Could we skip researcher and manually fetch a sample? Could fabricate? Not allowed to hallucinate.\n\nThus we must get researcher to run; need user approval. Let's re-run researcher and capture any approval request.\n\nWe'll run exec again and capture output; maybe the tool will include a special field. Use exec again.\n\n<thinking>Run researcher command again. Expect possible approval request.</thinking>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_1Oj2aSDhMc6GAYqeGkTrwM","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/researcher/sessions/sessions.json && openclaw agent --agent researcher --message \"Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Return the aggregated Single-Topic JSON.\" --deliver","timeout":120}}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0","usage":{"input":12268,"output":329,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12597,"cost":{"in