{"type":"message","id":"f5728921","parentId":"8291242f","timestamp":"2026-05-04T06:03:19.492Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Again killed. Possibly the exec environment disallows network. Maybe we need to set a flag to allow network? Not in spec.\n\nAlternate approach: Use curl fallback directly and bypass researcher agent. The SOUL says if researcher fails, try curl -s 'https://decrypt.co/feed' or 'https://coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/'. We could fetch those feeds and maybe assemble JSON manually, but we could just pass the raw RSS to writer? Writer expects RESEARCH_JSON. Might be okay to just provide minimal JSON with required fields (topic_theme, combined_key_facts, primary asset). We could fabricate a simple JSON based on fetched feed titles. That may be acceptable but we would be creating content. The policy says not to hallucinate; we can fetch real feed using curl (network). That also may need approval. We can request user approval for curl.\n\nLet's attempt curl -s 'https://decrypt.co/feed' to get RSS. Use exec, expect approval.\n\n<thinking>Run curl to fetch feed, may need network approval.</thinking>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_WELgH4iafWpjtECkCFqreZ","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s https://decrypt.co/feed","timeout":120}}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0","usage":{"input":12705,"output":251,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12956,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777874593740}}
{"type":"message","id":"c6a1f135","parentId":"f5728921","timestamp":"2026-05-04T06:03:19.936Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tooluse_WELgH4iafWpjtECkCFqreZ","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8' ?>\n<rss\n  version=\"2.0\"\n  xmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\"\n  xmlns:wfw=\"http://wellformedweb.org/CommentAPI/\"\n  xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n  xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\"\n  xmlns:sy=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/syndication/\"\n  xmlns:slash=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/slash/\"\n  xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\"\n  xmlns:snf=\"http://www.smartnews.be/snf\"\n>\n  <channel>\n    <title>Decrypt</title>\n    <description>What&amp;#039;s new in crypto and the advent of the decentralized web.</description>\n    <language>en</language>\n    \n    <atom:link\n      href=\"https://decrypt.co/feed\"\n      rel=\"self\"\n      type=\"application/rss+xml\"\n    />\n    \n    \n      \n        <link>https://decrypt.co/feed</link>\n      \n    \n    \n      <copyright>Decrypt Media</copyright>\n    \n    \n    \n    \n      <lastBuildDate>Sun, 03 May 2026 21:34:40 +0000</lastBuildDate>\n    \n    \n      <sy:updatePeriod>hourly</sy:updatePeriod>\n    \n    \n      <sy:updateFrequency>1</sy:updateFrequency>\n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n      <item>\n  <title>How Canton Network Lets Institutions Guard Against DeFi Security Risks: Digital Asset CEO</title>\n  <link>https://decrypt.co/366086/how-canton-network-lets-institutions-guard-against-defi-security-risks</link>\n  <pubDate>Sun, 03 May 2026 20:20:00 +0000</pubDate>\n  \n    <description>Because Canton allows participants to implement guardrails, Digital Asset&#39;s Yuval Rooz said institutions can protect against bad actors.</description>\n  \n  <dc:creator>André Beganski</dc:creator>\n  \n  \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://decrypt.co/?p=366086</guid>\n  \n  \n    <enclosure url=\"https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fill:1024:512:1:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/decrypt-style-wall-street-gID_7.png@png\" length=\"1000000\" type=\"image/png\" />\n  \n  \n    \n      <category>DeFi</category>\n    \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n    \n      <media:thumbnail url=\"https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/decrypt-style-wall-street-gID_7.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1280\"/>\n    \n    \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n\n\n</item>\n    \n      <item>\n  <title>You Installed Hermes. Now Make It Look Better Than ChatGPT or Claude</title>\n  <link>https://decrypt.co/366535/you-installed-hermes-make-look-better-chatgpt-claude</link>\n  <pubDate>Sun, 03 May 2026 19:55:35 +0000</pubDate>\n  \n    <description>The terminal is fine. But if you actually want to live in your Hermes agent, here are the four best GUIs the community has built—and how to run them.</description>\n  \n  <dc:creator>Jose Antonio Lanz</dc:creator>\n  \n  \n    <guid isPermaLink=\"false\">https://decrypt.co/?p=366535</guid>\n  \n  \n    <enclosure url=\"https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fill:1024:512:1:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/decrypt-style-hermes-green-gID_7.png@png\" length=\"1000000\" type=\"image/png\" />\n  \n  \n    \n      <category>Long Reads</category>\n    \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n    \n      <media:thumbnail url=\"https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/decrypt-style-hermes-green-gID_7.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1280\"/>\n    \n    \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n\n\n</item>\n    \n      <item>\n  <title>OpenAI GPT Image 2 vs Google Nano Banana 2: Which AI Image Generator Is Best?</title>\n  <link>https://decrypt.co/366408/openai-gpt-image-2-vs-google-nano-banana-2-review</link>\n  <pubDate>Sat, 02 May 2026 18:50:19 +0000</pubDate>\n  \n    <description>Which state-of-the-art AI image generator is most effective at producing A+ results? We put GPT Image 2 and Nano Banana 2 to the 